# Separator

Visually divides content with a one pixel line in the border color.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Separator } from "#lib/components/ui/separator/index.js";
</script>

<div>
	<strong>PlainSv</strong>
	<p>Svelte components styled with theme tokens.</p>
</div>
<Separator />
<nav>
	<span>Docs</span>
	<Separator orientation="vertical" />
	<span>Components</span>
</nav>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/separator.json
```

## Vertical

Set `orientation="vertical"` to draw a line between items in a row. It stretches to the height of its flex container, so give the row a height or content to fill.

<Demo section="vertical" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<div style="display: flex; gap: 1rem; height: 1.25rem">
	<span>Blog</span>
	<Separator orientation="vertical" />
	<span>Docs</span>
</div>
```

## Accessibility

By default, the separator is decorative and hidden from screen readers with `role="none"`. Set `decorative={false}` when it divides meaningful sections, so it is announced with `role="separator"` and, when vertical, `aria-orientation="vertical"`.

## API

The `Separator` props extend the native `div` attributes. It sets `data-orientation` for custom styles.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompProps<"div"> {
	/** Direction of the line; `vertical` stretches to the height of a flex row; defaults to `horizontal` */
	orientation?: "horizontal" | "vertical";
	/** Hides the line from screen readers when it is only visual; set `false` to announce it as a separator; defaults to `true` */
	decorative?: boolean;
}
```
